<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
# Phase 5 – Model Evaluation

This notebook evaluates the trained Random Forest model using the engineered EPL dataset. It includes metrics, reports, and visualizations that demonstrate model performance and feature importance.
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## Objective

Evaluate the final Random Forest model using the engineered dataset and capture performance metrics, classification reports, and model explainability outputs.
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
from pathlib import Path

import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import pandas as pd

from src.evaluate_model import ModelEvaluator

plt.rcParams["figure.figsize"] = (10, 6)
plt.rcParams["font.size"] = 11
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## Load engineered dataset
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
project_root = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
engineered_path = project_root / "data" / "processed" / "engineered_dataset.csv"
model_path = project_root / "models" / "random_forest_model.pkl"

evaluator = ModelEvaluator(
    dataset_path=engineered_path,
    model_path=model_path,
)

dataset = evaluator.load_dataset()
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## Load trained model
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
model = evaluator.load_model()
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## Dataset overview
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
print(f"Dataset shape: {dataset.shape}")
print(f"Numeric feature count: {dataset.select_dtypes(include=['number']).shape[1]}")

dataset.head()
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## Prediction
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
X, y = evaluator.prepare_data(dataset)
predictions = evaluator.predict(model, X)

print(f"Generated predictions for {predictions.shape[0]} observations.")

pd.Series(predictions).value_counts().sort_index()
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## Prediction probability
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
probabilities = evaluator.predict_probability(model, X)

print(f"Probability predictions shape: {probabilities.shape}")

y_scores = probabilities[:, 1]
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## Model metrics
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
metrics = evaluator.evaluate(y, predictions, probabilities)

metrics_summary = {
    key: value
    for key, value in metrics.items()
    if isinstance(value, (float, int))
}

metrics_summary
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
### Accuracy
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
print(f"Accuracy: {metrics['accuracy']:.4f}")
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
### Precision
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
print(f"Precision: {metrics['precision']:.4f}")
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
### Recall
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
print(f"Recall: {metrics['recall']:.4f}")
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
### F1 Score
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
print(f"F1 Score: {metrics['f1_score']:.4f}")
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
### Balanced Accuracy
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
print(f"Balanced Accuracy: {metrics['balanced_accuracy']:.4f}")
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
### ROC AUC
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
print(f"ROC AUC: {metrics['roc_auc']:.4f}")
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
### Matthews Correlation Coefficient (MCC)
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
print(f"MCC: {metrics['matthews_correlation_coefficient']:.4f}")
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## Classification Report
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
metrics['classification_report']
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## Confusion Matrix
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
metrics['confusion_matrix']
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## ROC Curve
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
roc_fig = evaluator.plot_roc_curve(y, y_scores)
plt.show()
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## Precision Recall Curve
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
pr_fig = evaluator.plot_precision_recall(y, y_scores)
plt.show()
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## Feature Importance
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
importance_df = evaluator.feature_importance(model, evaluator.feature_columns)
importance_df
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
feature_fig, feature_horizontal_fig = evaluator.plot_feature_importance(importance_df)
plt.show()
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## Save evaluation results
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="python">
saved_paths = evaluator.save_metrics(metrics)

for name, path in saved_paths.items():
    print(f"{name}: {path}")
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
## Summary & Key Insights

The model evaluation uses the engineered dataset and a previously trained Random Forest model. The results capture performance across classification metrics, confusion matrix, and prediction curves. Feature importance reveals the top predictors for foul win probability, while the classification report and confusion matrix help identify class imbalance behavior and areas for further improvement.
</VSCode.Cell>
